    retained: 'Explicit one-to-one problem-to-solution mapping; prayer anchoring; location-based Halal Radar; compromise and split engine; traveller and companion friction.',
    body: `<h2>Every pain has<br><em>a product response</em></h2><div class="mapping-layout"><div class="mapping-rows"><div><p class="small-label">Prayer blind spots</p><h3>Dynamic prayer anchoring</h3><p>Prayer windows and nearby facilities<br>become part of the shared day.</p></div><div><p class="small-label">Fragmented food search</p><h3>Location-based Halal Radar</h3><p>Nearby options show their evidence<br>and how they fit the trip.</p></div><div><p class="small-label">Conflicting group choices</p><h3>AI compromise & split planning</h3><p>Review a middle ground or parallel<br>activities with a regroup point.</p></div></div><figure class="friction-photo">${picture('prototype/mixed_group_struggle.jpg', 'Illustrative scene of a traveller checking a menu while a companion waits')}<figcaption>Illustrative scenario from the prototype</figcaption></figure></div>`,
    script: `Each of those problems maps directly to a Safar feature. Prayer blind spots become dynamic prayer anchoring: the window and nearby facilities are visible inside the day. Scattered food searches become location-based Halal Radar, with the available evidence beside each option. Conflicting choices become compromise and split planning. The group can choose a middle ground, or take a short separate activity and meet again. The image captures the situation we want to improve: one person anxiously checks a menu while a companion waits. Safar gives both people a plan they can review before that moment arrives.`,
    cue: 'Follow each problem directly into its named feature. The image is illustrative, not a photograph from a field study.',
