    body: `<h2>Malaysia as our launch hub<br><em>A business model to validate</em></h2><div class="business-layout"><div class="launch"><p class="small-label">Initial audience</p><h3>Malaysian friends<br>and student groups</h3><p>Start with outbound trips where halal food,<br>prayer and different interests need coordination.</p><div class="destinations"><div><b>Tokyo & Kyoto</b><span>Mixed-group holidays</span></div><div><b>Istanbul</b><span>City and cultural trips</span></div><div><b>Makkah & Madinah</b><span>Future faith-travel use cases</span></div></div></div><div class="revenue"><p class="small-label">Revenue hypotheses</p><div><b>Freemium / Pro</b><p>Test willingness to pay for advanced<br>group planning.</p></div><div><b>Travel-agency APIs</b><p>Explore licensing planning capabilities<br>to travel organisers.</p></div><div><b>Halal dining referrals</b><p>Explore partner commissions<br>with transparent recommendations.</p></div></div></div><p class="source">Proposed launch and expansion strategy. Paid demand, partnerships and revenue are not yet validated.</p>`,
    script: `Our proposed launch hub is Malaysia. We would begin with friend and student groups planning outbound trips, where the food, prayer and mixed-group coordination problem is easy to observe. Tokyo and Kyoto are our first demonstration setting. The wider direction includes city trips to Istanbul and, later, faith-travel use cases around Makkah and Madinah. The original business model has three paths: a freemium product with paid group-planning features, API licensing for travel agencies, and halal dining referral commissions. These are hypotheses to validate. First we want to see whether groups finish planning with less rework, resolve conflicts more clearly and return for another trip. That evidence should guide what we charge for and where we expand.`,
