const demoScript = `### Demo run sheet | 7:35–9:35

Prepare the guest Japan trip before presenting. Use a rehearsed live walkthrough or a two-minute recording of the same sequence. Do not wait for uploads or external services on stage. The slide provides the order. Press **B** for prepared screenshot fallbacks.

| Time | Action | Spoken line |
| --- | --- | --- |
| 7:35–8:00 | Open Ideas and the prepared social-link example. Show reviewed candidates, if available. | “A supported link becomes candidate places. We review the results before adding them to the group.” |
| 8:00–8:25 | Show Plan’s prayer window, then a Food evidence label. | “The prayer window sits inside the day. Food results show where the label comes from, so a traveller can decide what to verify.” |
| 8:25–9:05 | Show Ichiran in Ideas / Needs a decision. Inspect the warning and an alternative or regroup option. | “Here the group’s choice conflicts with food requirements. We can review a middle ground or a short split, with an agreed place to meet again.” |
| 9:05–9:25 | Show prepared booking fields or an existing hotel coverage warning. | “Reviewed booking details can expose a missing night or conflicting date before the group travels.” |
| 9:25–9:35 | Return to the deck. Advance to slide 12. | “The same trip connects discovery, prayer, group choice and booking review.” |

If no hotel gap exists in the prepared trip, show the current booking-completeness fallback and explain a checkout-before-flight gap as an example. The fallback shows missing journeys, not a detected hotel gap. If demo preparation is limited, keep the four beats as a narrated screenshot walkthrough within the same two minutes.
`;

const md = `# Safar finals pitch · 10 minutes

**Team Ds Gang:** Chong Pohyi, Teoh Xi Xian, Tan Wei Feng  
**Structure:** The prototype’s 12 sections, preserved in the original order. Expanded explanation runs to 7:35, followed by a two-minute demo and a 25-second close.  
**Deck:** [Open the HTML deck](finals-pitch.html). Keep it beside the assets folder for offline use.

The quoted passages below are spoken. Cues and source notes are for rehearsal. Timings are delivery targets, including pauses and handoffs, and need one full rehearsal at your natural pace.

## Timing and speaker handoffs

| Slide | Time | Topic | Suggested speaker |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
${slides.map((s,i)=>`| ${i+1} | ${s.time} | ${s.title} | ${i<4?'Chong Pohyi':i<8?'Teoh Xi Xian':'Tan Wei Feng'} |`).join('\n')}

## Spoken script

${slides.map((s,i)=>`### ${String(i+1).padStart(2,'0')} · ${s.title}\n\n**${s.time}**\n\n> ${s.script}\n\n**Cue:** ${s.cue}${s.source?`\n\n**Source:** ${s.source.split('\n').map(u=>`[Official source](${u})`).join(', ')}`:''}\n${i===10?'\n'+demoScript:''}`).join('\n')}

## Presentation controls

- Arrow keys or Space: move through slides. Home and End: first and last slide.
- **N**: full speaker notes. **F**: full screen. **T**: start or pause the ten-minute timer.
- **D**: demo slide. **B**: screenshot fallback. Click an image to enlarge it, then Escape to close.
- The deck works offline with its assets. The guest application and external source links need an internet connection.

## Prototype context checklist

| Prototype section | Preserved in finals |
| --- | --- |
${slides.map((s,i)=>`| P${String(i+1).padStart(2,'0')} / slide ${i+1} | ${s.retained} |`).join('\n')}

## Factual updates from the prototype

The original story and feature coverage stay intact. These wording changes keep the pitch aligned with available evidence and the current application:

- Market scale uses the sourced GMTI 2026 figures in slide 2. The old 1.8B, $230B, 160M and 10.5M figures had no embedded sources and are not repeated as current facts.
- The original Reddit examples remain. The 72%, 91% and 45-minute statements are not presented as measured research because their source and method were not supplied.
- Wanderlog and HalalTrip keep their place in the comparison. Their official feature descriptions replace absolute claims that no other solution exists or that HalalTrip has no prayer tools.
- Prayer calculations use the adhan library locally. Food labels show available evidence. Member and trip-lead review remain part of decisions, extracted document fields and resync proposals.
- “AI compromise & split planning” retains the original Auto-Split concept while making the approval step explicit. Safar does not automatically certify restaurants, decide visa eligibility or reissue transport tickets.
- Malaysia launch, destination expansion and the three revenue paths remain proposals. No user traction, paid demand or partnerships are implied.

## Q&A preparation

**What makes Safar distinctive?** It brings prayer windows, food evidence and mixed-group requirements into a shared planning decision, including a reviewed alternative or split with a regroup plan.

**What is live?** The deployed application and guest demo support shared trips, preferences, bookings, ideas and votes, food discovery and prayer-aware planning. External AI, places, weather and flight functions depend on configuration, quotas and provider availability.

**How do halal labels work?** Safar exposes the source and uncertainty of the evidence. A listed or likely result is different from certification evidence. Travellers confirm strict requirements with the venue.

**What happens when people disagree?** The app surfaces the reason and presents reviewable options. The trip lead chooses whether to accept, reserve, reject or apply a proposed plan.

**How will the team validate the business?** Start with real Malaysian mixed groups. Observe planning rework, missed constraints, successful conflict resolution and repeat use, then test willingness to pay or partner demand.

**What did the team learn during ideation?** Mentor feedback expanded a Muslim-only planner into a mixed-group workspace and showed why simple majority voting does not resolve strict requirements.

## Sources and visual provenance

- [Mastercard–CrescentRating GMTI 2026](${sources.market}) for market context.
- [Wanderlog official features](${sources.wanderlog}) and [HalalTrip official app page](${sources.halaltrip}) for the comparison.
- Project README and current source for implementation, limits and mentor history.
- Original prototype deck and its screenshots for the mobile concept, community examples, shared workspace, illustrative friction image and supporting-tool concepts. The deck labels historical concepts where they could otherwise look like current app evidence.
- Current user-guide screenshots for the Ichiran conflict and demo fallback screens.
`;

